evidence.quote:
Let $\mathcal T$ be a disjoint probability tree on a finite set $X$, with $k\ge1$ levels. Suppose that every level is $\sigma$-spread, where $\sigma>0$, and that its positive integer capacities satisfy $$\ell_{i+1}\ge16\ell_i\qquad(1\le i<k).$$ Set $$r=\min\{1,\;16\mathrm e^{50}\sigma(1+\log_2\ell_k)\}.$$ Then $$\mathbb P_{W\sim\mu_r}
 \bigl(\mathcal U(P)\subseteq W\text{ for some path }P\text{ of }\mathcal T\bigr)
 \ge\tfrac23.$$

