For every $n\ge2$ and every finite simple graph $H$ with $h=e(H)\ge1$ edges and at most $n$ vertices, $$\label{eq:stronger}
 p_{\mathrm c}(n,H)\le
 \min\{1,\;2048\mathrm e^{50}p_{\mathrm E}(n,H)(1+\log_2 h)\}.$$ In particular, $$p_{\mathrm c}(n,H)\le6144\mathrm e^{50}p_{\mathrm E}(n,H)\log_2 n.$$

Suppose that $|A_b|\le m$ for a positive integer $m$, the law $\nu$ is $a$-spread, and $$0<\rho<1,\qquad a/\rho\le\mathrm e^{-50}.$$ Let $W\sim\mu_\rho$, independently of the source choice, and perform the transition above. Call the transition a *local failure* if $$Z(Y)<\mathrm e^{-10m}\quad\text{or}\quad |T|>m/2.$$ Then $$\label{eq:local-failure}
 \mathbb P(\text{local failure})\le\mathrm e^{-9m}.$$ Moreover, for each fixed target $b$ and every nonnegative function $f$ depending only on $W\cap(X\setminus A_b)$, $$\label{eq:distortion}
 \mathbb E\!\left[
  \mathbf 1_{\{\mathrm{target}=b,\ Z(Y)\ge\mathrm e^{-10m}\}} f(W)
 \right]
 \le \mathrm e^{11m}\nu_b\,\mathbb Ef(W).$$ The expectation on the right is with respect to $W\sim\mu_\rho$.

