evidence.quote:
For every integer $d\ge3$, there exist constants $D<\infty$, $\varepsilon>0$, and finite connected pure $d$-dimensional simplicial complexes $X_m$, with $|X_m(0)|\longrightarrow\infty$, such that every vertex belongs to at most $D$ faces of dimension $d$ and, for every $f\in C^i(X_m;\mathbb F_2)$, $$\label{eq:goal}
 \norm{\delta_i f}_{X_m,i+1}
 \ge \varepsilon\,\operatorname{dist}_{X_m,i}(f,B^i(X_m))
 \qquad(0\le i<d).$$ The constants are independent of $m$, $i$, and $f$.

